# 3. Projectile Motion Calculator

```text
START

SET gravitational acceleration g = 9.81 m/s²

DISPLAY "Detailed Projectile Motion Calculator"

REPEAT FOREVER

    ASK user for initial velocity

    IF user enters "exit"
        EXIT program
    END IF

    ASK user for launch angle in degrees

    CONVERT angle from degrees to radians

    CALCULATE horizontal velocity
        vx = v × cos(angle)

    CALCULATE vertical velocity
        vy = v × sin(angle)

    CALCULATE total time of flight
        time_of_flight = (2 × vy) / g

    CALCULATE maximum height
        max_height = vy² / (2 × g)

    CALCULATE horizontal range
        horizontal_range = vx × time_of_flight

    DISPLAY total flight time
    DISPLAY maximum height
    DISPLAY horizontal range

    ASK user whether to check height at a specific time

    IF user enters a time
        CALCULATE height at that time
            height = (vy × t) - (0.5 × g × t²)

        IF t > time_of_flight
            DISPLAY that the object has already hit the ground
        ELSE
            DISPLAY height at the given time
        END IF
    END IF

IF invalid numerical input is entered
    DISPLAY "Error: Please enter numbers only."

END REPEAT

END
```

