# Notes

- The pseudocode describes the logic of the projects rather than Python syntax.
- The Molarity Calculator currently converts the moles input to a number before checking for the text `exit`, so the exit check needs to be fixed in the Python code.
- The Phone Number Details project currently uses a fixed `+91` input rather than asking the user for a number.
- The Time and Angle project calculates the time for 5 degrees, despite the original variable name/comment referring to 2 degrees.
